<title>USA: Key lawmaker doesn't see problem with Fed nominees.</title>
<headline>Key lawmaker doesn't see problem with Fed nominees.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senate Banking Committee Chairman Alfonse D'Amato has no reason to expect President Clinton's nominees to the Federal Reserve will run into any problems in the Senate, a spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But he added that the influential New York Republican lawmaker has yet to decide whether to support them.</p>
<p>Clinton said earlier that he would nominate University of Michigan professor Edward Gramlich and economic consultant Roger Ferguson to the central bank's board.</p>
<p>The nominations are subject to Senate confirmation and first must pass the Banking Committee that D'Amato heads.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
